error[E0277]: `i32` cannot be used as a primary-key argument for `user::Entity`
  --> tests/value_type_pk_compile_fail/raw_int_rejected.rs:33:38
   |
33 |     let _ = user::Entity::find_by_id(1i32);
   |                                      ^^^^ expected `user::Entity`'s `PrimaryKey::ValueType` (or something convertible to it), got `i32`
   |
   = help: the trait `FindByIdArg<user::Entity>` is not implemented for `i32`
   = note: type-safe `Id<E, _>` wrappers deliberately do not impl `From<inner>` to prevent cross-entity ID confusion. Construct ids explicitly with `Id::new(..)` (or the per-entity alias's `::new`), and pass an id belonging to this entity.
note: required by a bound in `find_by_id`
